-1) and did not reference real command IDs; this evaluation relies entirely on the raw command timeline and lifecycle snapshots rather than the executor's self-reported summary.\",\"It cannot be fully confirmed from the captured evidence whether the leftover dnsmasq 'hosts' entry on node2 causes any conflict with Unbound, since only unbound (port 53) was tested as the client-facing resolver; the dnsmasq entry appears unused but was not verified to be entirely inert.\",\"The scratch Python scripts left in /tmp on node2 were not confirmed via the temporary-files diff (which shows only auto-generated tmpcfd_* churn), so their persistence at task end is inferred from the absence of any removal command, not directly observed in the final snapshot.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"node1 (VyOS) resolves app.internal to node3's lan-a address for hosts on lan-a","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1's PowerDNS recursor was configured with a static-host-mapping for app.internal -> 10.50.10.12 (node3's lan-a IP) and bound to the lan-a interface (10.50.10.1). node3, configured to use node1 as its DNS server, successfully resolved app.internal to 10.50.10.12 via getent and pinged it successfully. The same resolution and reachability were re-verified after node1 and node3 were independently rebooted, confirming persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aa67ac4ea4204e00","cmd-f5c536c024704ce8","cmd-6761861cc0174d5a","cmd-1d007ea3d5984f20","cmd-f30b344a3194445a","cmd-9eeaaf83c0544554","cmd-8540332cdb154bb4","cmd-9943ba885f5342ef","cmd-21512a88f8034c56","cmd-cd37186a057849ae"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"node2 (OPNsense) resolves app.internal to node4's lan-b address for hosts on lan-b","status":"satisfied","summary":"After an initial misconfigured attempt via dnsmasq's config.xml structure, the executor added an Unbound host override (app.internal -> 10.50.20.12, node4's lan-b IP) and reconfigured Unbound, which listens on port 53 on the lan-b (opt1